{"1-7":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H7453","lemma":"רֵעַ","tr":"re·a","gloss":"neighbor","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":188},{"base":"H7326","lemma":"רוּשׁ","tr":"rush","gloss":"be poor","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":24},{"base":"H7227","lemma":"רַב","tr":"rav","gloss":"many","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":454},{"base":"H2896","lemma":"טוֹב","tr":"tov","gloss":"pleasant","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":538},{"base":"H2196","lemma":"זָעַף","tr":"za·aph","gloss":"to enrage","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H4976","lemma":"מַתָּן","tr":"mat·tan","gloss":"gift","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H4828","lemma":"מֵרֵעַ","tr":"me·re·a","gloss":"companion","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H5557","lemma":"סָלַף","tr":"sa·laph","gloss":"to pervert","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H0213","lemma":"אוּץ","tr":"uts","gloss":"to hasten","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H6141","lemma":"עִקֵּשׁ","tr":"iq·qesh","gloss":"twisted","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":11}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PRO","chapter":21,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"The plans of the diligent bring plenty, as surely as haste leads to poverty.","from":2},{"book":"PRO","chapter":29,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"Do you see a man who speaks in haste? There is more hope for a fool than for him.","from":2},{"book":"PHP","chapter":1,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"And this is my prayer: that your love may abound more and more in knowledge and depth of insight,","from":2},{"book":"PRO","chapter":28,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Better a poor man who walks with integrity than a rich man whose ways are perverse.","from":1},{"book":"PRO","chapter":14,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"The poor man is hated even by his neighbor, but many are those who love the rich.","from":4},{"book":"PRO","chapter":18,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"A manʼs gift opens doors for him, and brings him before great men.","from":6},{"book":"PRO","chapter":21,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"A lying witness will perish, but the man who listens to truth will speak forever.","from":5},{"book":"PRO","chapter":29,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Many seek the rulerʼs favor, but a man receives justice from the LORD.","from":6}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"8-14":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H3684","lemma":"כְּסִיל","tr":"ke·sil","gloss":"fool","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":70},{"base":"H1812","lemma":"דֶּ֫לֶף","tr":"de·leph","gloss":"dripping","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H2956","lemma":"טָרַד","tr":"ta·rad","gloss":"to pursue","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H5099","lemma":"נַ֫הַם","tr":"na·ham","gloss":"roaring","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H8588","lemma":"תַּעֲנוּג","tr":"ta·a·nug","gloss":"luxury","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H2197","lemma":"זַ֫עַף","tr":"za·aph","gloss":"rage","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H4079","lemma":"מִדְיָן","tr":"mid·yan","gloss":"contention","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H5000","lemma":"נָאוֶה","tr":"na·eh","gloss":"lovely","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H0802","lemma":"אִשָּׁה","tr":"ish·shah","gloss":"woman","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":781},{"base":"H6315","lemma":"פּוּחַ","tr":"pu·ach","gloss":"to breathe","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PRO","chapter":16,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":23,"source":"both","text":"He who is slow to anger is better than a warrior, and he who controls his temper is greater than one who captures a city.","from":11},{"book":"PRO","chapter":18,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":22,"source":"both","text":"He who finds a wife finds a good thing and obtains favor from the LORD.","from":14},{"book":"PRO","chapter":14,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":20,"source":"both","text":"A patient man has great understanding, but a quick-tempered man promotes folly.","from":11},{"book":"JAS","chapter":1,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":18,"source":"both","text":"My beloved brothers, understand this: Everyone should be quick to listen, slow to speak, and slow to anger,","from":11},{"book":"PRO","chapter":31,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":17,"source":"openbible","text":"A wife of noble character, who can find? She is far more precious than rubies.","from":14},{"book":"PRO","chapter":31,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":17,"source":"openbible","text":"Give her the fruit of her hands, and let her works praise her at the gates.","from":14},{"book":"COL","chapter":3,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":17,"source":"openbible","text":"Therefore, as the elect of God, holy and beloved, clothe yourselves with hearts of compassion, kindness, humility, gentleness, and patience.","from":11},{"book":"COL","chapter":3,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":17,"source":"openbible","text":"Bear with one another and forgive any complaint you may have against someone else. Forgive as the Lord forgave you.","from":11}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"15-23":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H5315","lemma":"נֶ֫פֶשׁ","tr":"ne·phesh","gloss":"soul","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":754},{"base":"H6098","lemma":"עֵצָה","tr":"e·tsah","gloss":"counsel","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":89},{"base":"H6066","lemma":"עֹ֫נֶשׁ","tr":"o·nesh","gloss":"fine","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H6103","lemma":"עַצְלָה","tr":"ats·lah","gloss":"sluggishness","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H8104","lemma":"שָׁמַר","tr":"sha·mar","gloss":"to keep: obey","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":469},{"base":"H8639","lemma":"תַּרְדֵּמָה","tr":"tar·de·mah","gloss":"deep sleep","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H5375","lemma":"נָשָׂא","tr":"na·sa","gloss":"to lift: raise","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":656},{"base":"H7649","lemma":"שָׂבֵעַ","tr":"sa·ve·a","gloss":"sated","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H4191","lemma":"מוּת","tr":"mut","gloss":"to die","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":840},{"base":"H6901","lemma":"קָבַל","tr":"qa·val","gloss":"to receive","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":13}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PRO","chapter":16,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":91,"source":"both","text":"A manʼs heart plans his course, but the LORD determines his steps.","from":21},{"book":"ISA","chapter":14,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":82,"source":"both","text":"The LORD of Hosts has sworn: “Surely, as I have planned, so will it be; as I have purposed, so will it stand.","from":21},{"book":"PRO","chapter":16,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":63,"source":"both","text":"The plans of the heart belong to man, but the reply of the tongue is from the LORD.","from":21},{"book":"PSA","chapter":33,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":52,"source":"openbible","text":"The LORD frustrates the plans of the nations; He thwarts the devices of the peoples.","from":21},{"book":"PSA","chapter":33,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":52,"source":"openbible","text":"The counsel of the LORD stands forever, the purposes of His heart to all generations.","from":21},{"book":"ISA","chapter":46,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":46,"source":"both","text":"I declare the end from the beginning, and from ancient times what is still to come. I say, ‘My purpose will stand, and all My good pleasure I will accomplish.’","from":21},{"book":"PRO","chapter":21,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":42,"source":"both","text":"There is no wisdom, no understanding, no counsel that can prevail against the LORD.","from":21},{"book":"EPH","chapter":1,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":39,"source":"both","text":"In Him we were also chosen as Godʼs own, having been predestined according to the plan of Him who works out everything by the counsel of His will,","from":21}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"24-29":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H3887","lemma":"לִיץ","tr":"luts","gloss":"to mock","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":28},{"base":"H1847","lemma":"דַּ֫עַת","tr":"da·at","gloss":"knowledge","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":92},{"base":"H0995","lemma":"בִּין","tr":"bin","gloss":"to understand","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":170},{"base":"H4112","lemma":"מַהֲלֻמֿוֹת","tr":"ma·ha·lum·mah","gloss":"blow","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H6747","lemma":"צַלַּ֫חַת","tr":"tsal·la·chat","gloss":"dish","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H6310","lemma":"פֶּה","tr":"peh","gloss":"lip","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":498},{"base":"H6191","lemma":"עָרֹם","tr":"a·ram","gloss":"be shrewd","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H1460","lemma":"גֵּו","tr":"gev","gloss":"back","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H6102","lemma":"עָצֵל","tr":"a·tsel","gloss":"sluggish","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"H8201","lemma":"שֶׁ֫פֶט","tr":"she·phet","gloss":"judgment","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":16}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PRO","chapter":21,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"When a mocker is punished, the simple gain wisdom; and when a wise man is instructed, he acquires knowledge.","from":25},{"book":"PRO","chapter":15,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"The way of the slacker is like a hedge of thorns, but the path of the upright is a highway.","from":24},{"book":"PRO","chapter":26,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"A whip for the horse, a bridle for the donkey, and a rod for the backs of fools!","from":29},{"book":"MRK","chapter":4,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"He went on to say, “Pay attention to what you hear. With the measure you use, it will be measured to you, and even more will be added to you.","from":27},{"book":"JOB","chapter":15,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"how much less man, who is vile and corrupt, who drinks injustice like water?","from":28},{"book":"PRO","chapter":10,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Wisdom is found on the lips of the discerning, but a rod is for the back of him who lacks judgment.","from":29},{"book":"1TI","chapter":6,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"If anyone teaches another doctrine and disagrees with the sound words of our Lord Jesus Christ and with godly teaching,","from":27},{"book":"1TI","chapter":6,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"and constant friction between men of depraved mind who are devoid of the truth. These men regard godliness as a means of gain.","from":27}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}